      "side": 1,
      "message": "It should not be possible to get to this point for an unimplemented offset, as in that case _plat__NvGetHandleVirtualOffset will return 0, and the TPM code will iterate through the real NV indexes looking for it. \n\nThat said - the _END and _MAX are confusing names, I think maybe it would be better if they were inverted.\n\n..and case in point, this should be checking \u003c _MAX (which is the end of the implemented/known indexes) - I\u0027ll update when I get into the office tomorrow morning..\n \nAlso yes, in future to implement support for undefined virtual indexes, this needs to change to return null (or more likely, a pointer to the static const 0-length config) and not assert",
